For future research, it is interesting to note, that in almost all cases the damage visualised on the glass surfaces at the pillars is found to be caused by macroscopic forces that stem from handling (i.e. transport or installation) or environmental loading (i.e. wind or thermal loads) during service life. In future investigations, the VDCNet could also be directly linked to well-defined mechanical models \citet{kocer2003} (e.g. the fracture mechanics of glass failure at pillar contacts). In linking the models, the imaging process could provide valuable information that would allow damage mitigation, which is a powerful pre- and post-production tool for quality control and ultimately safety in service of the VIG unit. In combination with an automated camera the imaging process will be faster and information about orientation as well as position of the camera then is also available.

